// Who is where, who owes whom, and what each kind of place means.

// ─── Kinds ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// A friend or a roommate. What they owe Alex is a claim on the place their entity points
/// to (a `receivable`), and what Alex owes them is a claim of theirs (a `payable`).
kind friend : entity

/// What a garden grant may pay for.
kind garden : expense


// ─── Me: money ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

account assets/bank/checking : bank
account assets/bank/savings  : bank

/// Cash in the wallet: tips in, small things out.
account assets/cash/wallet : cash

/// One card for everything, paid in full on the 22nd.
account liabilities/visa : credit-card


// ─── What people owe me, and what I owe them ────────────────────────────────
//
// A flow into a `receivable` with `due` makes a claim, and each is kept apart from the
// others by the flow that made it: a month's rent share, a bill's share, a loan, a trip.
// A payment `for #code` settles the claim the code marked, in part or in full. `axiom
// claims` lists what is still open, how old it is and when it fell due, and none of it
// counts as money to spend.

/// Ben: his thirds of the rent and the shared bills, and his share of the trip.
account assets/owed/by-ben : receivable

/// Cleo: the same.
account assets/owed/by-cleo : receivable

/// Riley: the loan, and a share of the trip.
account assets/owed/by-riley : receivable

/// The Lantern: what I bought for the job and am waiting to be paid back for. It is not income
/// when it arrives: it settles the claim.
account assets/owed/by-lantern : receivable

/// Ben pays the electricity, in his name: my third is what I owe him.
account liabilities/owed-to-ben : payable

/// Cleo's Costco runs: my third is what I owe her.
account liabilities/owed-to-cleo : payable


// ─── Income ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Pay and card tips from The Lantern, through payroll.
account income/wages : wages

/// Cash tips: taxable income when received (IRC §61), reported to the employer
/// monthly and to the IRS on the return.
account income/tips : wages


// ─── Expenses ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

account expenses/rent
account expenses/utilities
account expenses/groceries
account expenses/dining
account expenses/transport
account expenses/phone
account expenses/car
account expenses/health
account expenses/entertainment
account expenses/clothing
account expenses/gifts
account expenses/travel

account expenses/taxes/federal : federal-tax
account expenses/taxes/payroll


// ─── The collective ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Everything below belongs to green-table, not to me, though I am the one who
// enters it. The grant's money comes with strings (std's `grant` kind): it stays
// tied to the foundation in the collective's account, and may only be spent on
// places of kind `garden`, before the deadline.

/// The collective's account, opened with what earlier plant sales left.
account assets/bank/collective-checking : bank
  owner green-table

/// The cash box at events.
account assets/cash/collective-cash : cash
  owner green-table

account income/donations
  owner green-table
account income/grants
  owner green-table

/// Everything under here is a garden supply or a garden cost: the grant may pay it.
account expenses/garden/soil : garden
  owner green-table
account expenses/garden/seeds : garden
  owner green-table
account expenses/garden/lumber : garden
  owner green-table
account expenses/garden/irrigation : garden
  owner green-table
account expenses/garden/tools : garden
  owner green-table
account expenses/garden/fencing : garden
  owner green-table
account expenses/garden/water : garden
  owner green-table

/// Not a garden supply: the grant may not pay for it.
account expenses/volunteer-food
  owner green-table

/// The Riverfront Foundation's grant: 6,000.00 USD for garden supplies and
/// tools, to be spent by 2025-10-31. Money from it stays tied to it wherever it
/// lands; what is left at the deadline is owed back.
entity riverfront : grant
  via income/grants
  purpose garden
  until   2025-10-31


// ─── People and merchants ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// The Lantern, my employer. Pay arrives from `income/wages`.
entity lantern : employer
  via income/wages

/// The Lantern, as the one that owes me for what I bought for it.
entity lantern-owes : org
  via assets/owed/by-lantern

/// Ben and Cleo, my roommates, and Riley, a friend: each is a place people owe me on.
entity ben : friend
  via assets/owed/by-ben
entity cleo : friend
  via assets/owed/by-cleo
entity riley : friend
  via assets/owed/by-riley

entity landlord : org
  via expenses/rent
entity fiberco, power-co : org
  via expenses/utilities
entity costco, farmers-market : org
  via expenses/groceries
entity mint-mobile : org
  via expenses/phone
entity progressive, carmax-finance : org
  via expenses/car
entity marketplace-plan : org
  via expenses/health
entity mountain-cabins : org
  via expenses/travel
entity pizza-place : org
  via expenses/volunteer-food
entity hardware-hank, shed-co : org
  via expenses/garden/tools
entity water-dept : org
  via expenses/garden/water
entity bayview-soil : org
  via expenses/garden/soil
entity seed-savers : org
  via expenses/garden/seeds
entity northside-lumber : org
  via expenses/garden/lumber
entity drip-depot : org
  via expenses/garden/irrigation


// ─── Codes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// A month's rent share, a month's small shared bills (groceries and internet), a bill in
/// someone else's name, a loan and a trip: each code ties a payment to what it settles.
code rent-* shared-* trip-* loan-*
  on receivable

code power-* costco-*
  on payable

/// Something bought for the job and waiting to be paid back.
code expense-*
  on receivable
